{"name":"Programs: receive by flood","description":"Test demo: run a flood node, receive a signed program from the host nodes and run it","kind":"flood","entry":"flood.txt","args":["10.0.2.2:7012,10.0.2.2:7011","03e489240a78d8a85713f5b6d22749632d8268e238c40b9aca99f54c44de11828d","Downloaded: fib and primes"]}This app holds no program. It runs a programnetwork node, subscribes to the
nodes its args give, and waits for a have of the program its args name. It
downloads the program from the node that announced it, checks the signer
key of its args and every block hash, then runs the program.
See "DHT prototype (#18)" in docs/ProgramDistribution.md.
